#import "../template.typ": somatic_page

// PAGE 10: WHY SHADOW WORK FAILS - Critical insight before Phase 1
// Authoritative, clinical tone

#somatic_page(
  title: "Why Shadow Work Fails",
  body_text: [
    #rect(fill: rgb("#F5F5F0"), stroke: 0.5pt + gray, inset: 15pt, radius: 2pt)[
      Most shadow work fails because it remains theoretical. You journal about your triggers, you name your patterns, you even understand the origin of your wounds—and yet nothing changes. Why? Because *awareness is not transformation*. Insight without embodiment is entertainment.
      
      The shadow is not a concept to be understood. It is a *somatic holding pattern* that must be physically released. When you were shamed as a child, your nervous system did not file that experience in your prefrontal cortex. It *compressed it into your fascia*, tightened your diaphragm, and taught your body to collapse inward whenever vulnerability arose. That pattern is *pre-verbal, pre-cognitive*. You cannot think it away.
      
      This is the trap of "spiritual bypassing"—using insight as a substitute for integration. You say, "I know my father's anger taught me to people-please," and you believe that knowing is enough. But your body still flinches. Your jaw still clenches. Your belly still knots. The shadow has not been touched—only observed from a safe distance.
    ]
    
    #v(1cm)
    
    #align(center)[
      ◈ · ✦ · ◈
    ]
    
    #v(1cm)
    
    *The difference between intellectual and somatic shadow work:*
    
    - *Intellectual*: "I understand why I self-sabotage."
    - *Somatic*: "I feel the tightness in my throat when success approaches. I place my hand there. I breathe. I ask it: What are you protecting me from?"
    
    The shift is subtle but luminous. You stop analyzing and start *listening*. You stop fixing and start *feeling*. And slowly, the shadow stops hijacking you—because it has finally been heard.
    
    #v(1cm)
    
    The phases ahead will teach you this language. Not the language of therapy, but the language of alchemy. Not the language of insight, but the language of *transmutation*.
  ],
  image_path: none,
  layout_style: "bottom"
)
